WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.310
(bright music)

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:04.230
- When I'm running backwards,
it almost feels like I'm flying

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.850
because it's such a
different visual perspective,

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:12.850
seeing how far I've gone as
opposed to how far I need to go.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.670
When you're going backwards
you can really just

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:19.223
take a step back, literally,
and enjoy what you're doing.

00:00:24.513 --> 00:00:26.930
(playful music)

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.030
Hi, I'm Aaron Yoder.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.200
I'm a backwards runner.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.730
I have the world record for
the fastest mile ran backwards.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.335
My fastest backwards mile time is

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:39.193
five minutes and 54 seconds.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.520
I've been running forward
for over 20 years.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.180
I started running competitively

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.870
when I was in elementary school,

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.163
and then ran on scholarship
during my early twenties.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:57.083
I ran so much that I
sustained a knee injury.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.100
My doctor told me to stop running,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.240
and I really didn't wanna stop,

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.773
so I knew I had to make some sorta change.

00:01:05.773 --> 00:01:08.356
(upbeat music)

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:13.560
Retro running or
backwards running is where

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.380
you're literally just running in reverse,

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.040
and there's no impact on my knee.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.780
I run backwards everywhere.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.540
I run backwards on the treadmill,

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.540
I run backwards on the track,

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:26.463
and also out on country roads.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.190
Backwards running feels great on my knee

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.470
I don't feel anything,

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.133
which is a reason why I really enjoy it.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.220
Stay tall, knee up.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.053
There we go.

00:01:39.053 --> 00:01:40.213
Stand up, good job.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.160
When I'm coaching my track team,

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.260
I occasionally have them run backwards

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:48.990
as to enhance and diversify
their training workouts.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.410
Onward and upward, good job.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.930
Way to go, good warm up there.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:53.540
There's more backwards runners out there

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:54.430
than one would think.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:58.040
There are hundreds, if
not thousands, of people

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.750
that decide to run in reverse.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.550
The last World Championships there were

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:07.683
over 20 countries represented
and close to 200 athletes.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.300
Backwards running has
allowed me to see things

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.140
in a little bit different perspective.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.890
In a world where everyone goes forward

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:20.530
and I'm going backwards,
it's really allowed me

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:24.040
to just get back to
competing against myself

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.900
and not be so concerned
when other people are doing it,

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.720
and I found great
gratification in the fact that

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.449
I'm just competing against my own shadow.

00:02:32.449 --> 00:02:35.032
(bright music)

